This check fails when Laravel cannot find public/build/manifest.json, or when public/hot exists.
In your hosting File Manager:
1. Confirm these files exist:
   agencyos/public/build/manifest.json
   agencyos/public/build/assets/
   If missing, upload the entire public/build folder from your local project.
2. Delete agencyos/public/hot if it exists.
3. Set build folders to 755 and files to 644, then refresh /install.
Did you move the contents of agencyos/public into public_html? If yes, Laravel may be checking a different folder. Send the server paths for artisan and public_html/index.php so I can give you the exact path correction.

